# Committed build outputs (firmware + host binaries + slot apps + boot splashes).
#
# The repo-root .gitignore ignores *.uf2 globally; re-include ONLY the firmware
# image below. Other user content is NOT committed here: the ANIMATION keyframe
# UF2s stay local (tools/builds/ or flash partitions).
!firmware/ydkb_athena75_rgb_advanced_vial.uf2

# Beside it, uf2_common keeps the last ten builds under a timestamp. That is a
# local undo buffer, not something to ship, and the rule is on the directory so
# it holds for whatever else ends up in there.
firmware/history/

# Both packaged sim builds carry the firmware they boot in a Resources/ directory
# -- Contents/Resources inside the .app, beside the .exe in the Windows folder --
# and without this the committed copies have nothing to run.
!sim/**/Resources/firmware.uf2

# Slot apps (src/app/.gitignore ignores *.app under src/app/<name>/).
!apps/
!apps/*.app

# Local-only apps: ACE embeds the keyframe QGF built from private PNGs.
apps/ace.app
apps/hidden/

# Boot splashes (*.qgf is not ignored, so the two stock ones land here on their
# own). Everything under private/ is somebody's own artwork -- that is where a
# splash built from a picture you do not want in the repo goes.
boot/private/

# athena_sim (tools/build_sim.sh writes sim/<os>/). Committed like host_tool:
# every platform links the static SDL2 the script builds from source, so the only
# remaining dependencies are the ones the OS itself ships. What is committed is
# the desktop package and nothing beside it -- the executable inside it is also
# what the scripts run -- so a bare binary here is a leftover, not an output.
!sim/
sim/*/athena_sim
sim/*/athena_sim.exe
sim/*/athena_sim_cli
sim/*/athena_sim_cli.exe
!sim/readme.txt

# Only a build pointed at a shared SDL2 of your own (ATHENA_SDL2_DIR) leaves this
# beside the exe. Third-party binary: keep it local.
sim/*/SDL2.dll

# A window run saves the whole machine (F6) next to wherever it was started from,
# which for a double-clicked copy is inside the package. That is one person's
# session, not part of the package.
sim/**/*.state
